            <ArticleTitle>Morgagni's hernia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>43-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Congenital diaphragmatic hernias, including Morgagni s hernia, usually present in early childhood and are treated by surgical repair. This case report is about an unusual Morgagni s hernia, presenting with dyspepsia and chest pain, at the age of 45 years. For many years the diagnosis remained a dilemma because patient s chest x-ray was not done and she was treated for &quot;angina &quot; and &quot;dyspepsia&quot;. Diagnosis was obvious once a chest x-ray was done, however, barium studies were performed for further confirmation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
